  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory had strong medication-safety and handoff work, including repeated instructions not to change immunosuppression and a 1-week transplant follow-up plan. However, it closed without a complete required red-flag screen: the doctor covered several hepatic/infectious/renal danger signs, but no observable doctor turn screened dyspnea, night sweats, marked weight loss, or abdominal pain. It also only partially handled the privacy/minimum-necessary-sharing component of the family stigma conflict. These are minor/moderate responsibility-chain errors, so the deterministic cap is grade 2 despite later receipt and otherwise useful execution.",
